# THE BEACON IS SERVED VERBATIM, SO GIT MUST NOT REWRITE ITS LINE ENDINGS.
# assets/cw-events.js is a byte-for-byte carry of what cf-live serves at
# /js/cw-events.js, and build.py hashes the working-tree bytes to name it
# /assets/cw-events.<hash>.js. This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which is why
# every other tracked text asset in this checkout is CRLF in the working tree
# while its blob is LF: a fresh Windows clone would therefore serve a
# 6,194-byte CRLF beacon under a different hash from CI's 6,080-byte LF one --
# the same file, two URLs, and neither of them matching what production serves
# today. -text pins it.
#
# DELIBERATELY SCOPED TO THIS ONE FILE. assets/site.js and the six CSS bundle
# sources have the same problem and it is older than this line; widening the
# rule changes their bytes, therefore the bundle hash, therefore every page,
# and that is a content change for the owner to approve rather than a fix to
# smuggle in beside a beacon.
/assets/cw-events.js -text
